WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:04.550
Has this ever happened to you?

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.100
While glass and plastic can shatter and crack,

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.700
researchers have been hard at work developing

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.320
materials that can be easily reassembled,

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.020
using strings of molecules called polymers.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.480
Healable polymers are not a new idea,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.360
but previous versions were either soft, making

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.940
making them impractical for most applications,

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.880
or they required high temperatures

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.620
to merge the pieces back together.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.260
Using a pair of molecules linked together,

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.660
researchers have developed

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.320
a new kind of semi-transparent material,

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.620
that maintains both rigidity and healing properties,

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.820
without requiring any external heating.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.380
The key to this process lies in the design

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.420
of dense hydrogen bonds

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.399
that keep the polymer together.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.940
The hydrogen bonds form in a such a way

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.080
that the polymer doesn't crystallize,

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.520
giving the chains the ability to move freely,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.480
and combine when compressed.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.580
Different kinds of linkers were tested,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.440
such as TUEG2 and TUC8,

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.780
but the best-behaved was TUEG3.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.260
After being cut and gently compressed for 30 seconds,

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.840
a 2 square centimeter sheet can hold

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.760
300 grams of weight,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.500
roughly the same as a full can of soda.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.280
And the longer it’s compressed,

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.340
the stronger the bonds become.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.780
In the future, this rigid polymer could be

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.120
used to make robots and other technology

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.080
that can be easily repaired,

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.660
and maybe even let you fix a broken window.

